{
  "raw": {
    "https://cuny.jobs/F6D0B65DC4F64B21B296BA21585DDEE125": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Electrical Engineering",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Electrical Engineering. Assistant Professor - Electrical Engineering **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** The Department of Engineering & Environmental Science (EES) at the College of Staten Island of the City University of New York (CUNY) invites applications for a tenure-track position at the Assistant Professor level. The department is interested in an individual with a research focus and the ability to develop curricula related to Power Engineering and Renewable Energy Systems. Specifically, we seek candidates with research and teaching interests in electrical power generation, transmission, distribution, storage, and power electronics. The position is at the Assistant Professor level beginning August 25, 2027. The Department of Engineering & Environmental Science has a full-time faculty of 17, supplemented with over 15 part-time faculty members. It offers the Bachelor of Science degree (BS) in Engineering Science and the BS in Electrical Engineering (EE), and both degrees are ABET-accredited. The Engineering Science program offers two specializations usually taken in the junior and senior years for students to explore and prepare for particular areas of engineering. Specializations are in Computer Engineering and Mechanical Engineering (MechE). The department also offers BS degrees in Earth & Environmental Science and Earth & Environmental Science 7-12, a minor in Geology, an Associate in Science (AS) in Engineering Science (with EE and MechE specializations), as well as a Master of Engineering (ME) in Electrical Engineering and a Master of Science (MS) in Environmental Science. The PhD program in Environmental Science is administered by and through the CUNY Graduate Center, and the PhD programs in EE and Mech-E are administered through the City College of New York (CCNY), with which our department is in close collaboration. The successful candidate is expected to share responsibilities for advising students, serving on college committees, and handling departmental assignments (which include administrative, supervisory, and other functions). Recent funding to the department for power generation, offshore wind, and green energy has exceeded $2 million. The College of Staten Island (CSI) is a City University of New York (CUNY) senior college organized around two academic divisions and three schools, with over 10,000 students. CSI offers a broad range of academic programs in the liberal arts and sciences and in several professional areas. The College awards associate's, bachelor's, master's, and professional doctorate degrees, and in collaboration with The CUNY Graduate Center, numerous PhD degrees. CSI's internationally recognized faculty passionately engages in scholarly and artistic activities, and together with a strong professional staff, lead students through transformational learning experiences both inside and outside of the classroom. The College is situated on a 204-acre site, has recently incorporated a residential component, and is currently engaging in capital expansion. It is a hub of intellectual and artistic activity and a community partner and source of economic impact and job creation for the greater Staten Island area. **QUALIFICATIONS** Ph.D. degree in area(s) of experience or equivalent. Also required are the ability to teach successfully, demonstrated scholarship or achievement, and ability to cooperate with others for the good of the institution. Preferred qualifications include: + Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering or related field. + Demonstrated research interests in power engineering and renewable energy systems. + Postdoctoral or relevant industry experience in power engineering and renewable energy systems. + The candidate should be able to demonstrate an ability to successfully teach and mentor undergraduate and graduate students, have an established scholarship record, and have a willingness (and/or successful record) to apply for external funding/grants. + Good leadership skills to strengthen our ABET-accredited Electrical Engineering program. + Knowledge and/or willingness to learn and apply elements and tools of Artificial Intelligence (AI), machine learning in research area and/ or teaching is strongly encouraged. + Possess the credentials for appointment to the CUNY Graduate School Faculty of Electrical Engineering at CCNY. **COMPENSATION** $89,777 CUNYoffers facultyacompetitivecompensationandbenefits packagecovering health insurance, pensionand retirement benefits, paid parentalleave, andsavings programs. Wealsoprovidementoring andsupportfor research ,scholarship,and publicationaspartof ourcommitmenttoongoing faculty professionaldevelopment. **HOW TO APPLY** Visit www.cuny.edu, access theemployment page,loginor create anewuser account,and searchfor this vacancyusingtheJob ID#orTitle. Select \"ApplyNow\" andprovide the requested information. Candidates shouldprovideaCV/resumeandstatement ofscholarly interests. If you have difficulty with uploading multiple documents to the Website, please send them to : facultyrecruitsci@csi.cuny.edu **CLOSING DATE** November 8, 2026 **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32577 Location: College of Staten Island Job Type: Full-Time"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/9980C664EE154EB9B50EE83B7B32F7ED25": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Cinema Studies",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Cinema Studies. Assistant Professor - Cinema Studies **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** The Department of Media Culture at the College of Staten Island, City University of New York, invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Cinema Studies, with an anticipated start date of Fall 2027. The Department offers bachelor's degrees in Cinema Studies (with tracks in Production and Critical Studies) and Communication (with tracks in Corporate Communication, Design and Digital Media, Journalism, and Media Studies). The Department has a strong commitment to interdisciplinary inquiry and welcomes candidates whose work crosses traditional boundaries. We seek a candidate with the range to teach across both production and critical studies, grounded in a strong command of film and media history and theory. Given the rapidly evolving digital media landscape, the ideal candidate engages with diverse modes of production and brings a deep understanding of the craft alongside its social, cultural, political, and aesthetic dimensions. Candidates whose scholarship focuses on national, global, diasporic, African American, or LGBTQ+ cinemas are also welcome to apply. **QUALIFICATIONS** Candidates must hold an MFA or PhD. ABD candidates are eligible provided the degree is conferred prior to appointment. Preferred qualifications include: The successful candidate will have a demonstrated commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching as well as an active and developing research and creative practice. Candidates must demonstrate the ability to teach and mentor students in narrative, documentary, and experimental film and video production. The successful candidate will be expected to teach across these areas, advise senior production projects, and contribute actively to curriculum development and program review. **COMPENSATION** $73,294 - $85,556 CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** To apply, go to www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information.If you have difficulty with uploading your document to the website, or if you have any questions, please send them to facultyrecruithss@csi.cuny.edu Please send a cover letter, CV, statement of teaching philosophy, portfolio of creative and scholarly work, and names of three references in one single PDF. **CLOSING DATE** November 30, 2026 **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32372 Location: College of Staten Island Job Type: Full-Time"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/8D86CE63732047DAB840FC17E5CCDBB325": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Music Technology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Music Technology. Assistant Professor - Music Technology **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** The College of Staten Island, CUNY, seeks a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor, specializing in music technology. This position will develop and deliver a curriculum that integrates traditional and contemporary music technology methods, materials, and conceptual approaches. The ideal candidate will teach electronic music composition, audio production, and sound design courses; have advanced knowledge of industry-standard software and languages, such as Pro Tools, Logic Pro, Ableton Live, Max/MSP, etc.; and have knowledge of traditional sound design principles, theory, and history. The ideal candidate will play a key role in shaping a progressive curriculum that spans technical mastery, creative artistry, and cultural context, encouraging interdisciplinary collaboration and fostering connections with related disciplines such as sound design, film scoring, interactive media, and live event production. The ability to teach in a secondary area such as music theory, musicianship, musicology, or applied music would be welcome. The College of Staten Island is a four-year public institution within the City University of New York system. Ranked #33 in Top Performers in Social Mobility by _U.S. News and World Report_ , the College serves approximately 11,000 students, including undergraduates, graduates, and Ph.D.s, on a 200-acre campus. The Performing and Creative Arts Department, housed within the Division of Humanities and Social Sciences, includes Art History, Dance, Drama, Music, Photography, and Studio Art, serving approximately 200 majors, as well as delivering courses for General Education requirements. The department produces numerous performances and events for the campus and community each year, including a Festival of Electronic Music. Facilities consist of one large electronic-music studio with hardware and software for composition and sound design, and a recording studio. It is hoped that the successful candidate would work to secure funding for these facilities and oversee the renovation of the recording studio. **QUALIFICATIONS** Qualifications for the position are: an earned doctorate (Ph.D. or D.M.A.) in music composition, music technology, or a related field (candidates at the ABD level with exceptional credentials may be considered, provided the degree is conferred before appointment) Preferred qualifications include: Substantial record of ongoing research and/or creative practice, including premieres, grants, residences, and/or similar activities within the field, at the national and/or international level; a minimum of three years teaching experience at the college level as the teacher of record, preferably in electronic music or music technology topics; expertise in contemporary approaches, concepts, and critical issues as they pertain to electronic music composition and sound design, as well as fluency in the history of the discipline; knowledge of principles and methods for curriculum design, teaching, and instruction for students; and advanced communication (verbal, written and interpersonal) and organizational skills. **COMPENSATION** $73,294 - $85,556 CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** To apply, go to www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information.If you have difficulty with uploading your document to the website, or if you have any questions, please send them to facultyrecruithss@csi.cuny.edu. APPLICATION MATERIALS one page cover letter; C.V.; one page statement of teaching philosophy; two sample syllabi; contact information (email and phone number) for three professional references; All materials must be submitted as a single pdf, in the order listed. **CLOSING DATE** November 30, 2026 **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32375 Location: College of Staten Island Job Type: Full-Time"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/0EC266C143074E6A85C02131DD08586D25": {
      "title": "Lecturer or Doctoral Lecturer - Management",
      "description": "Lecturer or Doctoral Lecturer - Management. Lecturer or Doctoral Lecturer - Management **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** The Lucille and Jay Chazanoff School of Business of the College of Staten Island of the City University of New York invites applicants for a position as a Lecturer or Doctoral Lecturer in Management, beginning in the Fall semester of 2027. We seek candidates with outstanding teaching skills and commitments to serving the institution and its community. Primary responsibilities include graduate and undergraduate teaching and mentoring in Management subjects. Further responsibilities include committee and department assignments such as administration, supervision, and other functions. Specialization in Healthcare Management is of particular interest, but candidates with expertise in other aspects of management or entrepreneurship will also be considered. The College of Staten Island (CSI) is a City University of New York (CUNY) senior College organized around two academic divisions and three schools, with a total population approaching 12,000 students. The Chazanoff School of Business is accredited by AACSB and has approximately 1,900 majors, offering an AAS in Business; a BS in Accounting; a BS in Business with concentrations in Management, Marketing, Finance, and International Business; a BA and a BS in Economics; and a BS in Information Systems & Informatics in association with the Department of Computer Science. The School also offers an MS in Business Management with tracks in Strategic Management and Business Data Analytics, an MS in Accounting, an MS in Healthcare Management, and a Graduate Certificate in the Business Analytics of Large-Scale Data. Further information about the campus can be found at www.csi.cuny.edu/aboutcsi **QUALIFICATIONS** **MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS** PhD degree in area(s) of experience or equivalent (Doctoral Lecturer rank); Bachelors degree in area(s) of experience or equivalent (for Lecturer rank). Also required are the ability to teach successfully and to cooperate with others for the good of the institution. **OTHER QUALIFICATIONS** Preferred qualifications include an earned PhD or equivalent in Management or another appropriate area (for Doctoral Lecturer rank); knowledge of software applications relevant to the industry; and industry and teaching experience. **COMPENSATION** $87,149-$98,638 (Lecturer) $98,291-$100,899 (Doctoral Lecturer) CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Log on to www.cuny.edu, click on the \"About\" drop-down menu, choose Employment, then \"Search All Postings,\" and filter by College of Staten Island.\" Find Job ID #32726 and click on \"Apply Now.\" You will have to create or log in to a user account in order to apply. Candidates should provide a CV/resume, teaching or student evaluations if available, and statements on teaching philosophy and scholarly interests. Names, addresses and telephone numbers of at least three references should be included as part of the application. If you experience issues uploading supporting documents or applying, please send email to facultyrecruitbusiness@csi.cuny.edu prior to the closing deadline. **CLOSING DATE** December 6, 2026 **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32726 Location: College of Staten Island Job Type: Full-Time"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/D225BA8E17254AE9BCD268542761B28725": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate or Full Professor - Information Systems & Informatics",
      "description": "Assistant, Associate or Full Professor - Information Systems & Informatics. Assistant, Associate or Full Professor - Information Systems & Informatics **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** The Lucille and Jay Chazanoff School of Business of the College of Staten Island of the City University of New York invites applications for a **faculty member** in the **Information Systems and Informatics Program** **.** We seek candidates at the rank of **Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor** , depending on qualifications and experience, with outstanding teaching skills and evidence of a potential or distinguished record of scholarship, as well as a productive research agenda and a commitment to serving the institution and its community. Primary responsibilities include graduate and undergraduate teaching and mentoring in Information Systems subjects, with further responsibilities including committee and department assignments such as administration, supervision, and other functions. Specializations of particular interest include Artificial Intelligence (including but not limited to Machine Learning, Generative AI, Large Language Models, AI Agents, Trustworthy AI, AI Security, and Human-Centered AI), Cybersecurity, Data Science and Analytics, and Health Informatics. Candidates with expertise in **Systems Analysis, Software Development, and Enterprise Systems** will also be considered. The College of Staten Island (CSI) is a City University of New York (CUNY) senior College organized around two academic divisions and three schools, with a total population approaching 12,000 students. The Chazanoff School of Business is accredited by AACSB and has approximately 1,900 majors, offering an AAS in Business; a BS in Accounting; a BS in Business with concentrations in Management, Marketing, Finance, and International Business; a BA and a BS in Economics; and a BS in Information Systems & Informatics in association with the Department of Computer Science. The School also offers an MS in Business Management with tracks in Strategic Management and Business Data Analytics, an MS in Accounting, an MS in Healthcare Management, and a Graduate Certificate in the Business Analytics of Large-Scale Data. Further information about the campus can be found at www.csi.cuny.edu/aboutcsi **QUALIFICATIONS** PhD degree in area(s) of experience or equivalent. Also required are the ability to teach successfully, demonstrated scholarship or achievement, and ability to cooperate with others for the good of the institution. ABD applicants will be considered; however, their degree must be conferred prior to the first day of classes of fall 2027 in order to hold the position. Preferred qualifications include an earned PhD or equivalent in Information Systems, Computer Science, or other appropriate area, and a demonstrated commitment to research, publication, and teaching. **COMPENSATION** $94,017 - $114,091 (Assistant Professor) $113,745 - $134,808 (Associate Professor) $136,040 - $141,325 (Professor) CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Log on to www.cuny.edu, click on the \"About\" drop-down menu, choose Employment, then \"Search All Postings,\" and filter by College of Staten Island.\" Find Job ID #32725 and click on \"Apply Now.\" You will have to create or log in to a user account in order to apply. Candidates should provide a CV/resume and statement of scholarly interests. Names, addresses and telephone numbers of at least three references should be included as part of the application. If you experience issues uploading supporting documents or applying, please send email to facultyrecruitbusiness@csi.cuny.edu prior to the closing deadline. **CLOSING DATE** December 6, 2026 **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32725 Location: College of Staten Island Job Type: Full-Time"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/6DABFCC4016C4325AC774A859D50CAD125": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor - Nursing",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor - Nursing. Assistant or Associate Professor - Nursing **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** The College of Staten Island (CSI) is excited to announce a tenure-track open rank faculty position for the Nursing Department in Staten Island, New York. The Nursing Department is a member of the consortium of three senior City University of New York (CUNY) colleges that offer undergraduate and graduate nursing degrees. The College of Staten Island offers two prelicensure programs (AAS and 4-year BS), as well as the RN-BS, Masters (Nurse Practitioner and Clinical Nurse Specialist) and Doctor of Nursing Practice (Advanced Clinical Care) programs. This open rank position is for a dynamic faculty member eager to collaborate and teach in undergraduate and graduate curricula. The CSI nursing faculty position presents an exceptional opportunity for the successful candidate to participate in the continued intellectual and institutional growth and development of the long-standing Nursing Department within the City University of New York. This position is anticipated to begin in Fall 2027 and is a full-time, in-person teaching position. Generally, full-time faculty at CUNY (except library faculty) have annual leave from the day after spring commencement until three days, excluding Saturday and Sunday, before August 30. CSI is a senior CUNY college organized around two academic divisions and two schools with over many professional areas. CSIs internationally recognized faculty passionately engage in scholarly and artistic activities, and together with a strong professional staff, lead students through transformational learning experiences both inside and outside of the classroom. The college is situated on a 204-acre tree-lined spacious site with recently built student dormitories and is currently engaging in capital expansion. CSI is a hub of intellectual and artistic activity, a community partner, and source of economic impact and job creation for the greater Staten Island area. The colleges faculty, administration, and staff are committed to educational excellence as they instill in students an enduring love of learning and respect for pluralism and diversity. The college community recognizes its responsibility to strive for the common good, including an informed appreciation for the interdependence of all people, and providing students with opportunities for successful careers. The successful candidate will have a graduate degree in nursing. Other qualifications include the ability to teach successfully and provide service; commitment to academic and inclusive excellence; strong communication skills; and the ability to cooperate with others for the good of the institution. **QUALIFICATIONS** **_Required Qualifications:_** + Doctoral degree in nursing (PhD, EdD, or DNP). If earned doctorate is not in nursing, must have a masters degree in nursing. + New York State license as a registered nurse, unencumbered, with current registration. If not licensed and registered in New York State, must have an unencumbered registered nurse license in another state in the United States and be eligible to obtain licensure in New York State following hire. + Three (3) years of clinical nursing practice + Three (3) years of academic teaching experience with nursing students in classroom and clinical sites. **_Preferred qualifications include:_** 1. Advanced Practice Registered Nurse certification and experience. 2. Evidence of professional scholarship activities in nursing such as research, publications, quality improvement projects, conference presentations. 3. Experience in writing grants 4. Knowledge of simulation standards of best practice. 5. Experience with academic accreditation and writing curricular reports. **COMPENSATION** Assistant Professor: $59,256 - $98,231 Associate Professor: $76,848 - $113,745 *Salary commensurate with education and experience. CUNY offers competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. Generally, full-time faculty at CUNY (except library faculty) have annual leave from the day after spring commencement until three days, excluding Saturday and Sunday, before August 30. Salary is distributed over 26 pay periods annually. **HOW TO APPLY** Visit www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create an new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. Candidates should provide a CV/resume and statement of scholarly interests. If you have difficultly with uploading multiple documents to the Website, please send them to: facultyrecruitsci@csi.cuny.edu **CLOSING DATE** December 6, 2026 **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32685 Location: College of Staten Island Job Type: Full-Time"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/DBE90B61DDF5407F8F1D0A163B79B45525": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Finance",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Finance. Assistant Professor - Finance **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** The Lucille and Jay Chazanoff School of Business of the College of Staten Island of the City University of New York invites applicants for a position as an Assistant Professor in Finance, beginning in the Fall semester of 2027. We seek candidates with outstanding teaching and research skills and commitments to serving the institution and its community. Primary responsibilities include graduate and undergraduate teaching and mentoring in Finance subjects. Further responsibilities include committee and department assignments such as administration, supervision, and other functions. Specializations of particular interest include Corporate Finance and Financial Markets. Candidates with expertise in data analysis and other aspects of finance will also be considered. The College of Staten Island (CSI) is a City University of New York (CUNY) senior College organized around two academic divisions and three schools, with a total population approaching 12,000 students. The Chazanoff School of Business is accredited by AACSB and has approximately 1,900 majors, offering an AAS in Business; a BS in Accounting; a BS in Business with concentrations in Management, Marketing, Finance, and International Business; a BA and a BS in Economics; and a BS in Information Systems & Informatics in association with the Department of Computer Science. The School also offers an MS in Business Management with tracks in Strategic Management and Business Data Analytics, an MS in Accounting, an MS in Healthcare Management, and a Graduate Certificate in the Business Analytics of Large-Scale Data. Further information about the campus can be found at www.csi.cuny.edu/aboutcsi **QUALIFICATIONS** PhD degree in area(s) of experience or equivalent. Also required are the ability to teach successfully, demonstrated scholarship or achievement, and ability to cooperate with others for the good of the institution. ABD applicants will be considered; however, their degree must be conferred prior to the first day of classes of fall 2027 in order to hold the position. **OTHER QUALIFICATIONS** Preferred qualifications include: an earned PhD or equivalent in Finance or Economics or other appropriate area; knowledge of financial markets, investment analysis, and corporate finance; and industry and/or teaching experience. **COMPENSATION** $94,017 - $102,460 CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Log on to www.cuny.edu, click on the \"About\" drop-down menu, choose Employment, then \"Search All Postings,\" and filter by College of Staten Island.\" Find Job ID #32724 and click on \"Apply Now.\" You will have to create or log in to a user account in order to apply. Candidates should provide a CV/resume and statement of scholarly interests. Names, addresses and telephone numbers of at least three references should be included as part of the application. If you experience issues uploading supporting documents or applying, please send email to facultyrecruitbusiness@csi.cuny.edu prior to the closing deadline. **CLOSING DATE** December 8, 2026 **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32724 Location: College of Staten Island Job Type: Full-Time"
    },
